Perfect! All tests are now passing. The bug was a classic off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). This caused:

1. `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
2. `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError since there's no second element

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first word from the split string.
